# Jekyll build output
_site/

# Ruby bundler artifacts. Gemfile.lock is gitignored because the
# github-pages gem pins transitive deps tightly; lock-file churn in CI
# is noisy without correctness benefit. bundler-cache in the GHA
# workflow + the github-pages pin in Gemfile deliver reproducible
# builds without committing the lock.
Gemfile.lock
.bundle/
vendor/bundle/

# Stale brand logos and working zips at repo root.
# Root-only ignore by extension (the leading slash anchors to repo root,
# so subdirectories like Publication-Images/, icons/, etc. are unaffected).
/*.svg
/*.png
/*.webp
/*.jpeg
/*.jpg
/*.zip

# Whitelist root-level images that must stay at repo root (referenced as
# absolute paths from the live site: favicon (browser tab) and
# apple-touch-icon).
!/apple-touch-icon.png
!/favicon.png
!/favicon.svg

# Defensive ignores added 2026-04-26 post-partition cleanup.
# Workflow content that re-accumulated in this site clone has been moved
# to the workflow clone (CryptoZach/Claude1) per partition logic. These
# patterns prevent re-accumulation in this site clone going forward.
.files/
scripts/.deps/
Cryptozach-site-files/

# .claude/ IS NOT PUBLIC. Author directives 2026-08-14: "memory mirror shouldnt
# ever go to public repo, only private repo (Claude1)" and ".claude/worktrees
# should not be in public repo, only claude1 private". This reverses the note
# that stood here until 2026-08-14, which described .claude/memory/ as "the
# git-tracked auto-memory backup" of THIS repo.
#
# Ignored as a WHOLE DIRECTORY rather than subdirectory by subdirectory, because
# enumerating them is a game you lose once: .claude/memory/ and
# .claude/worktrees/ were the only two ever tracked here, and a third would have
# ridden in silently exactly as those did.
#
# THIS IS THE WEAKER HALF, written down so nobody mistakes it for the fix.
# gitignore does not apply to ALREADY-TRACKED files, and 41 memory files are
# still tracked here, so this alone would stop new files and let every edit to
# those 41 through. The real enforcement is scripts/hooks/pre-commit, which
# blocks any staged ADDITION under .claude/ and defeats `git add -f` (verified
# 2026-08-14 by a live probe commit that was rejected). Deletions stay allowed
# there on purpose, so this can be cleaned up later without disarming the guard.
#
# The 41 memory files remain tracked and public at HEAD by author decision;
# removing them from HEAD would not unpublish them from history anyway. The
# .claude/worktrees/97344 gitlink WAS untracked, since it carried no content:
# an unmapped mode-160000 pointer to a commit in this same repo.
#
# NOTE for whoever needs to re-include something under .claude/ later: you
# cannot. A negation like `!.claude/foo` has NO effect once the DIRECTORY is
# excluded, because git never descends into it to evaluate the exception. To
# carry one file you must ignore narrower paths instead of `.claude/` itself.
.claude/
